-## Reproducibility and limits
+The June 2, 2003 reply asserts that records showed the United 93 hijack was reported at **0916L**. The January 2004 recording's provisional machine passages describe a possible assumption about a tail number at **916** and an interjection identifying it with **175**. The **1316** ledger entry is consistent with the tail-number alternative. It gives no Flight 93 identifier. The staff monograph reads the entry at **9:16** and cites NEADS Identification Technician **Channel 5 at 9:16:19** for a corresponding call. The acquisition did not establish the exact log Marr used or acquire or align that underlying channel segment. Keep the June claim, the qualified later account and the actual row distinct. [June email counterparts](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/77ee92f829c0be9c4360dc4d8ab3ef8410537281/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-marr-scott-paper-counterparts-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Interview audio locator](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/19799a41f9cfdd97fcb26323a525753ac1f4d5cd/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-marr-recording-speech-locator-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Staff monograph, section 8.3 and note 148](https://www.rutgerslawreview.com/wp-content/uploads/special/911/Sept11_Monograph.pdf)
 
